    "summary": "Jacquard woven blanket in the &#039;Moshoeshoe&#039; design, in russet, grey and black, with four vertical &#039;pin stripes&#039; in white. Four images of King Moshoeshoe I, one in each corner of the blanket, are based on the etching by Eugène Casalis. Four winged Sotho shields, with crossed clubs and spears, create the shape of a Victoria Cross in the centre of the design. Two images of Mount Qiloane near Moshoeshoe&#039;s mountain stronghold, Thaba Bosiu, run along two opposite edges of the blanket.",
